<h1>k<sup>th</sup> shortest path</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The problem of finding the k<sup>th</sup> <a href="shortestpath.html"><em>shortest path</em></a> from one <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertex</em></a> in a <a href="graph.html"><em>graph</em></a> to another vertex.  Variants may require that paths are edge- or vertex-disjoint, that is sharing no <a href="edge.html"><em>edges</em></a>  or vertices.  "Shortest" may be least number of edges, least total  weight, etc.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="shortestpath.html"><em>shortest path</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

